<title>UNITED NATIONS: Iraq's Aziz says U.S. blocking oil-for-food deal.</title>
<headline>Iraq's Aziz says U.S. blocking oil-for-food deal.</headline>
<dateline>UNITED NATIONS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iraq's Deputy Prime Minister Tareq Aziz charged the U.S. with blocking full implementation of the oil-for-food accord during a speech at the United Nations Earth Summit on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The oil-for-food agreement has not led to a tangible improvement of the situation yet. The agreement has not been implemented in fact due to suspending of a large number of the contracts for food, medicine and civilian needs by the American delegation in the Sanctions Committee,&quot; Aziz said.</p>
</text>
